Overlay patch 0035: async Metal shader compilation (reference 0035 / 2ship D-008, device-validated). Cold newLibrary+newRenderPipelineState blocks the render thread ~120-160ms per shader on A-series -> area-transition freezes. Register the program shell + draw-read fields synchronously (draws bind it immediately, LoadShader before dispatch), run the compile on a detached thread (gSohIos.AsyncShaders, default ON, live kill switch via bridge cvar), publish each pipeline with a release fence, and SKIP draws whose pipeline is not ready yet (they pop in a few frames later). Fork adaptations vs reference: GetInstance (no GetRawInstance), no sRGB (unconditional BGRA8Unorm), extra prg fields (SHADER_PALETTE_TEXTURE, usedLighting), library/function null-guards preserved inside the lambda as release-and-return. Compile ledgers (lib_ms/pso_ms) via extern C readers. __IOS__-only; the #else keeps the pristine synchronous path.

